# A meter-parametric lambda plus 827 Poitou--Tate engine

The first pointed Poitou--Tate implementation fixed its wild local state to
the explicit W1 receipt.  The genuine cyclotomic audit later showed that
this particular state has power-one character, whereas the irregular
reflected meter must have power-44 character.

The Poitou--Tate mechanism itself does not depend on that representative.
This file extracts it for an arbitrary actual roots-valued local Kummer
meter.  Its wild carrier is the smallest submodule containing all genuine
reflected global localizations and the supplied meter.  Global reciprocity
proves `range <= kernel`; the reverse inclusion remains the visible PT
exactness seam.  A cancelling state produces only an existential global
lift, and the unique allowed normalization freedom is retained as a unit
wild scale.

No meter is selected here, no character law is assumed, and no action,
provider, reciprocity law, or PT exactness theorem is manufactured.
-/
